{
  "_note": [
    "Absent keys mean labelled false, zero or not present. Only the perspective",
    "section is written exhaustively, because its None-vs-unspecified distinction",
    "cannot be inferred from absence.",
    "GATING: the love_interest_* fields are gated on relational_focus_present and",
    "NOT on relationship_is_romantic. The spec's gate is relational focus, not",
    "romance, so these fields are populated -- and non-null -- for a friendship, a",
    "bereavement or a folktale focus too, wherever the song centres on one specific",
    "other. The key name asserts romance; the data does not mean it. The spec fixes",
    "the column names, so this note is the fix.",
    "They are null, never false, exactly when relational_focus_present is false.",
    "LANGUAGE: cast-agreement is Italian, the only non-English song. Grammatical",
    "agreement cannot be expressed in English, so without it that casting mechanism",
    "would have no case at all. Its agreement figure is measured on one song in a",
    "language the spec does not validate, and must be reported with that caveat",
    "rather than counted as validation."
